  "_doc": "M7 G-C1: AI difficulty preset registry. 5 archetypes (rifleman/sniper/assault/engineer/medic) × 3 difficulties (cakewalk/tough_crowd/veteran) = 15 archetype-specific entries. Each entry carries archetype_id + difficulty_id + display name + M2 legacy AI tuning fields (hp, aim_settle_ticks, miss_chance, sight_range, sight_fov_degrees, hearing_radius, memory_decay_ticks, reload_ms, retreat_hp_pct) + M7 friend-feedback normalized multipliers (hp_multiplier, damage_multiplier, reaction_time_ticks, fov_degrees, hearing_range) + the three M7 spec extension fields. Values scale per archetype role: Sniper has the largest cover-seek radius (96u tough_crowd baseline) for high-ground search; Assault has the smallest (32u) for aggressive close-quarters; Medic has the highest retreat HP fraction (0.45 tough_crowd baseline) to stay alive and triage allies; Assault has the lowest (0.20) to commit aggressively. Squad comm delays mirror archetype radio discipline (Sniper slowest, Assault fastest). hp_multiplier ranges 0.75 (cakewalk) -> 1.0 (tough_crowd) -> 1.5 (veteran); damage_multiplier 0.75 -> 1.0 -> 1.4. The cf-ai builtin() fallback still resolves the three legacy ids (cakewalk/tough_crowd/veteran) for engines that load the M2 baseline shape.",
